The code statements that fix the bug are:
chg->charger = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &pm8916_lbc_charger_psy_desc, &psy_cfg);
ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, irq, NULL, pm8916_lbc_charger_state_changed_irq,
                                IRQF_ONESHOT, "pm8916_lbc", chg);
Reason:
By moving the `devm_request_threaded_irq` call to after the `devm_power_supply_register` call, the allocation order ensures that during removal the IRQ is disabled (freed) before the power supply is unregistered. This eliminates the race condition because the interrupt handler will never be invoked after the `power_supply` handle becomes invalid. Additionally, during probe the power supply is fully initialized before the IRQ is enabled, preventing access to an uninitialized handle.

